# Close-out D6 (owner ruling OD-8): `platform-migrate create-first-admin` refuses a login whose platform user exists and is inactive. The fault disables that refusal in the command; the real binary then makes the inactive user the first admin (exit 0) and the harness test must say so.
GATE=first-admin-inactive
TARGET=platform
SETUP=
STEP=go test TestCloseoutFirstAdmin_RefusesAnInactiveExistingUserAndWritesNothing (the command refuses an inactive platform user, writes nothing)
CMD=H_PG_ADMIN_DSN="$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" bash tests/harness/run-db-tests.sh '^TestCloseoutFirstAdmin_RefusesAnInactiveExistingUserAndWritesNothing$'
MESSAGE=--- FAIL: TestCloseoutFirstAdmin_RefusesAnInactiveExistingUserAndWritesNothing
MESSAGE=an inactive existing platform user: exit 0, want 1
